      "instruction": "Setback frame with an upper left cantilever\n\nReconstruct geometry and connectivity from the architectural input.dxf, interpreting its S-* structural lines and labels while filtering the A-* wall, column-footprint and equipment distractors. Reconcile the labelled orthographic views using properties.json dxfMapping. Read supports from properties.json boundaryConditions and the CAD annotations; use the matching member labels in assignments.json and loads.json. Section-detail images describe section properties and roll only. Member local direction follows DXF LINE start-to-end as specified in properties.json; no structural geometry image is supplied. Perform first-order linear elastic analysis using OpenSees; save the self-weight OFF and no-rigid-diaphragm settings. Use explicit section/material stiffness and signed right-handed global axes, Z upward. Retain actual load positions and distributed loads.\n\nReport all of the following for each stated selection, with signs and units:\n- Upper left free tip: Uz [case-D-tip-uz]\n- Upper left column at its top: M2 [case-D-uc0-j-M2]\n\nProvide labelled model and result figures consistent with the numerical values. Preserve the input-to-model ID mapping, engine version/settings, current execution log, original result tables and figure data. If an essential datum is missing, ask specifically for it before analysis.\n",
